Chapter: UnitFieldAssign
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Field assignment through a unit wrapper is refused at CHECK, with the
 same code as the access half.

 This path already failed at CHECK before 2026-07-28, so the change
 here is not the refusal but WHAT IT SAID. It raised two diagnostics
 and both were false:

   CDX2060  Field assignment requires a mutable record; '' is immutable
   CDX2005  Record type has no field 'x'

 The record is declared `mutable`, and it does have that field. The
 empty name in the first is the same missing strip: the type-name
 lookup reads RecordTy and ConstructedTy and answers "" for anything
 else, so the wrapper produced a message about a type with no name.

 **What this test CANNOT check, stated so nobody reads more into a
 green than is there.** A `.failing` sidecar requires each listed code
 to appear; it cannot require that no OTHER code appears. So this pin
 catches the refusal disappearing or changing code, and it would NOT
 catch CDX2060 and CDX2005 coming back alongside it. The single-
 diagnostic property was verified by hand on the compiler that shipped
 this change and is not under a runner.

Section: Types

  mutable Point = record {
   x : Integer,
   y : Integer
  }

  Spot = unit Point

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let s = Spot (Point { x = 7, y = 9 })
    in act
      s.x = 5
      print-line-uni "done"
    end
  end
